      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::015::3_3_1_potentiodynamic_polarization_test"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Additional grain boundaries provide more nucleation sites for oxidation in the passivation layer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::015::3_3_1_potentiodynamic_polarization_test"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increasing surface grain-boundary density accelerates passivation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::015::3_3_1_potentiodynamic_polarization_test"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain refinement promotes formation of a continuous, uniform, adherent iron-oxide film.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::015::3_3_1_potentiodynamic_polarization_test"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain refinement produces a thicker and less defective passivation film.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::015::3_3_1_potentiodynamic_polarization_test"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The improved passivation film acts as a barrier that slows subsequent corrosive attack.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::015::3_3_1_potentiodynamic_polarization_test"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperature, diffusion along refined grain boundaries accelerates formation and improves the uniformity of the protective oxide layer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated coarse-grained Q235 steel forms a patchy, nonuniform, and less protective oxide scale.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain-refined Q235 steel will have lower corrosion current density than untreated Q235 steel.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain-refined Q235 steel will have a more uniform and adherent oxide scale than untreated Q235 steel.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10744552::web::015::3_3_1_potentiodynamic_polarization_test"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain-refined Q235 steel will exhibit less localized corrosion, including less pitting, than untreated steel.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted corrosion benefit applies at both room temperature and approximately 300 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed benefit requires oxygen-rich, moderately corrosive conditions in which an iron oxide can form.",
